course: dictionary
lesson: 13948
title: Liability: owing money and being responsible
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A liability is something you are legally responsible for, especially paying for damage or harm. Read the words around it to find the meaning. «The car park says: no liability for lost bags.» The clue is the sign: the car park is not responsible if your bag is lost.
explain: In money, liabilities are the things a company or person owes. «The shop lists its assets and its liabilities.» Assets are what it owns. Liabilities are what it must pay back, so they are the opposite of owning something.
explain: In everyday talk, a liability is a person or thing that causes problems. «Sam keeps dropping the ball, so the coach says he is a liability.» The clue is the problem he causes, so a liability is someone who can let the team down.
fact: Liability means being legally responsible, especially for paying for damage or harm.
fact: Liabilities are the money a person or company owes.
fact: «Assets and liabilities» means what you own and what you owe.
fact: In everyday speech, «a liability» is a person or thing that causes problems or puts others at risk.
fact: Signs saying «no liability» mean the owners will not pay if something is lost or damaged.
exercise: «The car park sign says: no liability for loss or damage.» What does no liability mean? | *The owners are not responsible for paying for damage | The car park is closed | Cars must park on the grass | The owners will pay for everything
exercise: A company lists its assets and liabilities. What are liabilities? | Its shop windows | *Money the company owes | Things the company owns | Its best workers
exercise: The coach says, «Sam is a liability to the team.» What does liability mean here? | A new team kit | A winning player | A fast runner | *A person who causes problems
test: Which word means money a person or company owes? | Asset | Team | Pool | *Liability
test: «She agreed to accept liability for the broken window.» What does accept liability mean? | Lose the key | Refuse to pay anything | Count the money | *Agree to be responsible for paying
exam: «A careless driver who crashes often is a liability on the road.» What does liability suggest? | A kind of car | A prize for careful driving | A map of the roads | *A risk that puts others in danger
